1. To search any word using wild character *
 =>  ls file1.* < it will search everything starts with file1
 =>  ls *.pdf   <  it will search everything ends with .pdf
2. to create  multiple files/folder
=> touch linux{1..30}.pdf < it will create Linux1 to Linux 30 in one go
=> ls linux*.*   < it will list all files start with linux.
=> rm linux{1..10}.pdf < it will remove files contains linux1 to linux10 only
3. To search single character
=> ls ?123  < it will list the string with123 in one character
=> ls ????? < it will search only 5 character strings/numbers
=> ls [abcde]*  < it will list all files that contains  a,b,c,d,e
=> ls *[1-9]*   < it will list all files contains numeric values from 1 to 9
=> ls *[a-z]*   < it will list all files which contains a to z values
=> ls test??  < it will list files which start with list and after list it contains 2 characters 
=> ls | grep -v 'a' < it will list all files which does not contain character a
=> ls | grep -v 'test' < it will list all files which doesnot contain test
4. Switch to last workind directory 
=> cd -
5. To run multiple commands in a single go 
 => ls; pwd; free -m
